1,,Epic,E-001 Customer Ordering,"Everything a customer does before paying: finding a restaurant, building a cart, placing an order and keeping an account.",High,,R-001,R-002,R-003,R-011,R-012,
2,,Epic,E-002 Payments and Live Tracking,"Taking the payment securely, moving the order through its states and keeping the customer informed until delivery.",High,,R-004,R-005,R-006,R-012,R-013,
3,,Epic,E-003 Restaurant and Courier Operations,The tools restaurant staff and couriers use to run their side of an order.,High,,R-003,R-007,R-008,R-009,,
4,,Epic,E-004 Platform and Reliability,"Build pipeline, monitoring, performance and end-to-end verification so the service can launch and stay up.",High,,R-011,R-013,,,,
5,1,Story,"S-001 Search and browse nearby restaurants by cuisine, name or dish","As a hungry customer, I want to search and browse nearby restaurants by cuisine, name or dish, so that I can quickly find something I want to eat.

Acceptance criteria:
- The restaurant list shows only restaurants that deliver to the customer's location, sorted by distance by default.
- Customers can filter by cuisine and search by restaurant or dish name.
- A menu shows each item with a photo, price and description; unavailable items are greyed out and cannot be added.
- Search and menu pages respond in under 2 seconds at the 95th percentile.",High,16,R-001,R-011,sprint-1,sprint-3,,
6,1,Story,S-002 Add dishes to a cart and place an order for my delivery address,"As a customer, I want to add dishes to a cart and place an order for my delivery address, so that the food is prepared and brought to my door.

Acceptance criteria:
- A cart holds items from one restaurant only; adding an item from another restaurant asks the customer to start a new cart.
- The cart shows item totals, the delivery fee and the order total, and updates them as quantities change.
- Checkout requires a delivery address and accepts an optional note to the restaurant.
- If an item becomes unavailable or its price changes, the customer is told before the order is placed.",High,13,R-002,sprint-1,sprint-2,,,
7,1,Story,S-003 Register and sign in with my email and password,"As a new user, I want to register and sign in with my email and password, so that my addresses and order history are saved.

Acceptance criteria:
- A user can register with an email address and a password of at least 10 characters.
- Passwords are stored only as salted hashes and sessions expire after 30 days of inactivity.
- Signed-in customers can save, edit and delete delivery addresses and view past orders.
- Restaurant staff and couriers sign in through the same service and only see their own tools.",High,10,R-003,R-012,sprint-1,sprint-2,,
8,2,Story,S-004 Pay for my order by card or digital wallet,"As a customer, I want to pay for my order by card or digital wallet, so that my order is confirmed without handling cash.

Acceptance criteria:
- Card details are entered in the payment provider's hosted fields and never reach our servers.
- An order is sent to the restaurant only after the provider confirms the payment.
- A declined payment shows a clear message and keeps the cart so the customer can retry.
- A payment confirmation is shown on screen and sent by email, and duplicate webhooks never charge or confirm twice.",High,16,R-004,R-012,sprint-1,sprint-2,,
9,2,Story,S-005 Watch my order progress and see the courier on a map,"As a customer, I want to watch my order progress and see the courier on a map, so that I know when to expect my food.

Acceptance criteria:
- The order page shows the current status: placed, accepted, preparing, picked up, delivered or cancelled.
- While the order is on the way, the courier's position on the map refreshes at least every 10 seconds.
- The page updates without a manual refresh and recovers after a dropped connection.
- An accepted order and its status history are stored durably and survive a service restart.",High,15,R-005,R-013,sprint-1,sprint-2,,
10,2,Story,S-006 Be notified when my order changes status,"As a customer, I want to be notified when my order changes status, so that I do not have to keep the app open.

Acceptance criteria:
- A notification is sent when the order is accepted, picked up and delivered.
- Customers can choose push, SMS or email, and can switch notifications off.
- A failed notification is retried and never blocks the order from moving forward.",Medium,3,R-006,sprint-2,,,,
11,3,Story,"S-007 Edit my menu, prices and item availability","As a restaurant manager, I want to edit my menu, prices and item availability, so that customers always see what I can really serve.

Acceptance criteria:
- A manager can add, edit and delete menu items with name, description, photo and price.
- An item can be switched to unavailable with one action and is immediately greyed out for customers.
- Menu changes are visible to customers within one minute.
- Only staff of that restaurant can change its menu.",High,8,R-003,R-007,sprint-2,sprint-3,,
12,3,Story,S-008 See new orders and accept or reject them with a preparation time,"As a restaurant staff member, I want to see new orders and accept or reject them with a preparation time, so that I stay in control of the kitchen's workload.

Acceptance criteria:
- A new paid order appears in the inbox within 5 seconds and plays a sound until it is answered.
- Staff can accept an order with a preparation time, or reject it with a reason.
- An order that is not answered within 3 minutes is cancelled and the customer is refunded.",High,5,R-008,sprint-2,,,,
13,3,Story,"S-009 Receive delivery offers, accept one and update its status","As a courier, I want to receive delivery offers, accept one and update its status, so that I can pick up and deliver orders efficiently.

Acceptance criteria:
- When an order is accepted, nearby available couriers receive an offer showing pickup, drop-off and earnings.
- The first courier to accept gets the job; the others see it disappear.
- The courier marks the order picked up and delivered, and the app shares the courier's position while the job is active.
- If no courier accepts within 5 minutes, operations staff are alerted.",High,13,R-009,sprint-3,,,,
14,4,Story,"S-010 Automated deployment, monitoring and load testing","As a platform operator, I want automated deployment, monitoring and load testing, so that ordering stays fast and available as traffic grows.

Acceptance criteria:
- Every merge to the main branch is built, tested and deployed to a staging environment automatically.
- Error rate, latency and queue depth are visible on a dashboard, and an alert fires when ordering fails for 5 minutes.
- A load test of search and checkout confirms the 2-second p95 target before release.
- An end-to-end test covers the full order journey from sign-in to delivery.",High,18,R-011,R-013,sprint-2,sprint-3,sprint-4,
